From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:31:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] AML: the film waits for HFR VRR to be on

HFR VRR is entered after the stereo mode changes, outside the refresh rate
change the player waits for (11_25), so a 3D film could start its sound
just before the switch to 1080p 165 Hz dropped it. The codec says the
switch is coming while HFR VRR is wanted and not yet on.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/AMLCodec.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/AMLCodec.cpp
@@ -2891,6 +2891,7 @@
   // A failed read (-1, e.g. connector not connected) is not an enabled core.
   bool dv_enabled(AmlDisplay->aml_get_drmProperty("dv_enable", DRM_MODE_OBJECT_CRTC) > 0);
   CLog::Log(LOGDEBUG, "CAMLCodec::CloseDecoder");
+  m_processInfo.SetDisplayChangePending(false);
 
   SetPollDevice(-1);
 
@@ -4079,6 +4080,8 @@
     CWinSystemAmlogic::RequestFs3dCheck();
   }
   const bool fs3dPending = fs3dWanted && !m_fs3dActive;
+  // the player starts the film once HFR VRR is on, not into the switch
+  m_processInfo.SetDisplayChangePending(fs3dPending);
   RenderStereoView guiStereoView = CServiceBroker::GetWinSystem()->GetGfxContext().GetStereoView();
   if (m_guiStereoView != guiStereoView)
   {
